St. Columba Food Pantry: Guide for Neighbors and Volunteers

The food pantry is in the lower level of the parish center, entered from the parking lot.

The food pantry is open Wednesdays from 4:00 pm to 6:30 pm and on the third Saturday of each month from 9:00 am to 11:00 am.

Any household in the Harrow Falls school district may visit once a week. Please bring a piece of mail with your address on your first visit.

The pantry is coordinated by Bertrand Oyelaran, who schedules volunteers and places the monthly order with the regional food bank.

Volunteers must be at least 14 years old. Volunteers under 18 serve with a parent or guardian.

Item | Most needed
Protein | canned chicken, peanut butter, dried beans
Breakfast | oatmeal, shelf stable milk
Personal care | diapers size 4 and 5, toothpaste
